    "result_text": "The test passes. Let me summarize the full-stack change I made.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 *\"on a client's page show me how many projects and contacts they have\"* \u2014 is now implemented as a small, additive, full-stack feature. The e2e test passes.\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor REST):** a new `GET /api/clients/summary?clientId=<id>` endpoint returning per-client counts.\n- `ClientSummary.java` \u2014 a record `(projectsCount, contactsCount)`.\n- `ClientSummaryRepository.java` \u2014 a `@Repository` running two `COUNT(*)` queries scoped by `client_id`.\n- `ClientSummaryGetLogic.java` \u2014 the logic class (`@HttpQueryParameter(\"clientId\")` + `ObjectResponse`).\n- `rest/api/clients/summary.GET.yml` \u2014 one new YAML wiring the endpoint (under `/api/` so it bypasses the SPA fallback).\n\n**Front-end (React):**\n- `ClientSummary.tsx` \u2014 a new component that owns its own state, fetches the summary, and renders the counts on the anchors the spec asserts: `client-projects-count` and `client-contacts-count`.\n- `ClientsPage.tsx` \u2014 composed the new component into the opened-client view (two-line import + render additions, no central-router edits).\n\n**Database:** no migration was needed \u2014 the counts are read-only aggregates over the existing `projects` and `contacts` tables, so no schema change was warranted. Everything else stayed additive and local per the project rules; no `data-testid` was renamed or removed, and no pinned scaffolding or the test spec was touched.\n\nVerification: `bin/e2e` \u2192 `1 passed` (project count `2`, contact count `3`).",
